# Written by every local `graphify query`. CI's own extract step never reads
# or writes it, so a fresh query here is disposable state, not part of the
# graph CI commits.
#
# NOTE: this repo's initial public-release commit accidentally committed a
# copy, so this line alone does not stop `git status` reporting it modified
# after a query -- .gitignore has no effect on an already-tracked path. The
# matching `git rm --cached` is a separate, blocked follow-up (see
# branchLeft/workspace#303 and its linked hook-guard issue): the PreToolUse
# guard that keeps an agent from ever committing graphify-out/ content has no
# carve-out for a deliberate untrack, so the commit gets refused. This line
# is forward-prep -- it takes effect the moment that untrack lands.
graphify-out/cache/last_query_stamp

# This repo tracks package-lock.json (seven of them) and CI runs `npm ci`; a
# pnpm install here is a mistake, and its lockfile must not get committed.
pnpm-lock.yaml
pnpm-workspace.yaml
